ts associated with prescription drug cost-sharing among poor and elderly persons</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>285</volume><fpage>421</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11242426</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040283-b008"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lexchin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Grootendorst</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Effects of prescription drug users fees on drug and health services use and on health status in vulnerable populations: A systematic review of the evidence</article-title><source>Int J Health Serv</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>122</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15088676</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040283-b009"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anis</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Guh</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacaille</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Marra</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rashidi</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>When patients have to pay a share of drug costs: Effects on frequency of physician visits, hospital admissions and filling of prescriptions</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><volume>173</volume><fpage>1335</fpage><lpage>1339</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16301701</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040283-b010"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hsu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Brand</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surna